WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.978
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.028 --> 00:00:05.405
Tiny Coders, video 3.

3
00:00:05.455 --> 00:00:08.180
Patterns you can repeat.

4
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.700
Patterns help you predict what comes next — and later, write shorter programs.

5
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.458
Red, blue, red, blue — what comes next?

6
00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:21.029
Blue.

7
00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:26.058
Clap, stomp, clap, stomp — the pair repeats.

8
00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:31.430
Three, six, nine, twelve — add three each time.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.296
Some lists have a repeating rule.

10
00:00:35.346 --> 00:00:37.105
Others are just random.

11
00:00:37.155 --> 00:00:41.746
Coders look for the piece that repeats so they do not write

12
00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:43.240
it again and again.

13
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.019
Let us recap.

14
00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:49.179
A pattern repeats with a rule.

15
00:00:49.229 --> 00:00:53.077
Finding the rule helps you plan code.

16
00:00:53.127 --> 00:00:55.710
Next: Loops: do it again.
